{
  "_comment": [
    "PNP dev-baseline policy (PEI-598) — the first enforced Peios firewall",
    "policy, now with the Flow layer (rung 2). The kernel reads",
    "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules whole at registryd's registration, re-walks",
    "on change, and publishes it as a policy generation; applying this seed",
    "flips enforcement ON at boot.",
    "",
    "The compiled-in backstop is DROP for every layer, both directions,",
    "always (ratified): every rule below is a visible, deletable permissive",
    "statement, per the doctrine that permissiveness never lives in",
    "defaults. Shape approved by jack 2026-09-02:",
    "",
    "  RawPacket  all            Matches everything, passes: the wire-proximate",
    "                            layer ships no policy, visibly.",
    "  Packet     tracked        The cheap per-packet filter passes every",
    "                            tracked packet (new, established, related);",
    "                            the Flow layer judges new flows once, and the",
    "                            flow's sentence answers for the rest. What is",
    "                            untracked (conntrack-invalid) hits the backstop.",
    "             outbound-ok    Untracked outbound (ND, ARP replies) passes.",
    "             loopback       Localhost is policed like everything else;",
    "                            every local daemon depends on this rule.",
    "             arp            PNP polices ARP where stock Linux never did.",
    "             icmpv6-housekeeping  ND (133-137) and MLD (130-132, 143) ride",
    "                            outside conntrack; IPv6 dies quietly without them.",
    "             dhcp-client    OFFER/ACK can arrive as broadcast conntrack will",
    "                            not tie to the DISCOVER's flow.",
    "  Flow       outbound-ok    Every flow this machine originates passes — the",
    "                            ratified shipped posture until the identity tier",
    "                            earns outbound strictness.",
    "             loopback       A loopback flow has two endpoints; the inbound",
    "                            one needs its own yes.",
    "             dev-viewer-ports  DEV-ONLY: atrium-server (8080) and the pnpd",
    "                            viewer (8081) stay reachable through QEMU",
    "                            hostfwd. Delete the day this baseline grows up.",
    "",
    "Everything else inbound answers to the Flow backstop, once per flow.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the kernel package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\RawPacket" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\RawPacket\\all",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet\\tracked",
      "values": [
        { "name": "FlowState.Equal", "type": "multi", "data": ["new", "established", "related"] },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet\\outbound-ok",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Direction.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "out" },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet\\loopback",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Interface.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "lo" },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet\\arp",
      "values": [
        { "name": "EtherType.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "arp" },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet\\icmpv6-housekeeping",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Protocol.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "icmpv6" },
        { "name": "IcmpType.Equal", "type": "multi", "data": ["130-137", "143"] },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Packet\\dhcp-client",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Protocol.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "udp" },
        { "name": "SrcPort.Equal", "type": "dword", "data": 67 },
        { "name": "DstPort.Equal", "type": "dword", "data": 68 },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Flow" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Flow\\outbound-ok",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Direction.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "out" },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Flow\\loopback",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Interface.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "lo" },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Network\\Rules\\Flow\\dev-viewer-ports",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Direction.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "in" },
        { "name": "Protocol.Equal", "type": "sz", "data": "tcp" },
        { "name": "DstPort.Equal", "type": "multi", "data": ["8080", "8081"] },
        { "name": "Actions", "type": "multi", "data": ["PASS"] }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
